title: a2.1 Daily Walk
syntax: xwiki/2.1
%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
**Abstract.** Seven stakeholders have a stake in the daily walk. Four walk: the resident with dementia (ST-01), the care worker who escorts them (ST-02), a fellow resident who joins as walking partner (ST-04) and a volunteer who walks with residents one-to-one (ST-07). Three shape the walk without walking: family (ST-03), care home management (ST-05) and medical and therapy staff (ST-06). They share an interest in the resident's physical and mental health, and differ on how far freedom of movement may be traded for safety.

= Stakeholder - Resident with dementia [ST-01] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-01
|Name|Resident with dementia
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01, SA-03, SA-04.
|Type|Direct - walks, exercises
|Values and motivations|(((
* Well-being (high) - physical and mental health
* Autonomy (high) - chooses whether, where and how fast to walk
* Safety (high) - no falls, no getting lost
* Social connectedness (medium) - company on the walk
* Dignity (medium) - accompanied, not guarded
* Privacy (medium) - whereabouts known only to those who need them
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Escorted by ST-02 or ST-07, sometimes by ST-03. Walks with ST-04. Lives under ST-05's exit and outdoor-access rules. Mobility and fall risk assessed by ST-06.

== Graph edges ==

performs → SA-01, SA-03, SA-04; appears-in → PS-01, PS-02, PS-03.

= Stakeholder - Care worker [ST-02] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-02
|Name|Care worker
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01 to SA-04.
|Type|Direct - escorts walks, handles incidents
|Values and motivations|(((
* Safety (high) - every resident back, unharmed
* Well-being (high) - residents get daily exercise
* Attentive care (high) - time for each resident despite other care tasks
* Autonomy (medium) - lets residents choose, within time and safety limits
* Privacy (medium) - for residents, and against surveillance of own work
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Escorts ST-01; pairs ST-01 with ST-04. Coordinates ST-07. Employed by ST-05. Informs ST-03 of incidents. Follows ST-06's exercise and fall-risk advice.

== Graph edges ==

performs → SA-02; supports → SA-01, SA-03, SA-04; appears-in → PS-01, PS-02, PS-03.

= Stakeholder - Family member [ST-03] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-03
|Name|Family member
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01.
|Type|Indirect - walks with the resident at times
|Values and motivations|(((
* Safety (high) - fears falls and the resident leaving the home
* Well-being (high) - physical and mental health of their relative
* Dignity (high)
* Autonomy (medium)
* Privacy (low) - may want more information on whereabouts than the resident would share
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Relative of ST-01. Occasional walking companion. In contact with ST-02; may consent on ST-01's behalf.

== Graph edges ==

supports → SA-01.

= Stakeholder - Walking partner [ST-04] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-04
|Name|Walking partner
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-04.
|Type|Direct - fellow resident, walks with ST-01
|Values and motivations|(((
* Social connectedness (high) - company on the walk
* Well-being (high) - own physical and mental health
* Autonomy (high) - free to decline or end a joint walk
* Dignity (medium) - partner, not helper
* Privacy (medium) - shares the walk, not personal information
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Fellow resident of ST-01, often with dementia too. Matched by ST-02. Has own family (ST-03) and care plan (ST-06).

== Graph edges ==

performs → SA-04; appears-in → PS-02.

= Stakeholder - Care home management [ST-05] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-05
|Name|Care home management
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01, SA-02.
|Type|Indirect - sets exit and outdoor-access policy, staffing; decides on adoption
|Values and motivations|(((
* Safety (high) - liable when residents leave unnoticed or fall
* Attentive care (high) - staffing and workload
* Well-being (high) - quality of care
* Autonomy (medium) - open versus locked doors
* Privacy (medium) - data protection for residents and staff
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Employs ST-02; screens and insures ST-07. Responsible for the building, garden and exits used by ST-01 and ST-04.

== Graph edges ==

governs → SA-01 (exits, outdoor access), SA-02 (staffing).

= Stakeholder - Medical and therapy staff [ST-06] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-06
|Name|Medical and therapy staff: GP, nurse, physiotherapist
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01, SA-03.
|Type|Indirect - assesses mobility, sets exercise programme
|Values and motivations|(((
* Well-being (high) - mobility, physical and mental health
* Safety (high) - fall risk
* Autonomy (medium)
* Privacy (medium) - medical confidentiality
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Assesses mobility and fall risk of ST-01 and ST-04. Advises ST-02 on exercise.

== Graph edges ==

supports → SA-03 (exercise programme); appears-in → PS-03.

= Stakeholder - Volunteer [ST-07] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-07
|Name|Volunteer
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01, SA-04.
|Type|Direct - unpaid, walks with residents one-to-one
|Values and motivations|(((
* Social connectedness (high) - personal bond with the resident
* Well-being (high) - resident enjoys the walk
* Safety (high) - unsure how to handle disorientation, falls or exit-seeking
* Autonomy (medium) - own schedule, free to stop volunteering
* Privacy (medium) - for residents; no access to medical information
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Walks with ST-01, or with ST-01 and ST-04 together. Coordinated by ST-02. Screened and insured by ST-05. Relies on ST-02 for advice from ST-06.

== Graph edges ==

supports → SA-01, SA-04; appears-in → PS-02.
